```bash
cat > /tmp/feature_documentation.md << 'EOF'
## Configurable Certificate Renewal Window Ratio

The PKI module now supports configuring the certificate renewal window ratio. This ratio determines how early before expiration a certificate should be renewed.

### Configuration

In your Caddy configuration, you can now specify the `renewal_window_ratio`:

```json
{
  "pki": {
    "renewal_window_ratio": 0.3,
    "certificate_authorities": {
      "local": {
        // ... your CA configuration
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The value should be a float between 0 and 1, representing the percentage of the certificate's lifetime after which renewal should begin.
For example, a value of 0.3 means certificates will be renewed when they reach 70% of their lifetime (30% before expiration).

If not specified, the default value of 0.2 (20% before expiration) is used, maintaining backward compatibility.
EOF
```

